  // Submit page
  "submit.title": "List your provider",
  "submit.intro": "Connect the wallet for your registered FTSO address, sign to prove you control it, then fill in your details. Your provider page is available right away; new providers list in the feed 30 days after claiming (see below).",
  "submit.manage.title": "Manage your listing",
  "submit.manage.intro": "Sign in with your provider address to edit your details, update your logo, or link another network. Edits take effect right away. (A new provider still inside its 30-day hold appears in the feed once the window ends.)",
  "submit.manage.loading": "Loading your listing…",
  "submit.reg.title": "On-chain registration is required first",
  "submit.reg.body": "You must already be a registered FTSO signal provider on Flare or Songbird before you can list here. Flare Registry does not register you with Flare; it reads your existing on-chain registration. If your address is not yet registered as an FTSO entity, register on-chain first, then come back to list. Note: new providers are held from the listed feed for 30 days after claiming (a review window for the Management Group) before listing automatically.",
  "submit.qual.summary": "What does it take to be Qualified?",
  "submit.qual.intro": "Listing and the {qualified} badge are different. Your provider page is available as soon as you sign in, but new providers are held from the listed feed and the Qualified badge for 30 days after claiming, so the Management Group can review before you reach wallets. After that window you list and show Qualified automatically once you meet the criteria, unless the Management Group has opened a case, which holds you until it concludes (providers listed before this policy are unaffected). Qualified is computed automatically from Flare's on-chain reward data, and is shown as a transparent checklist on your provider page. To be Qualified you must meet all of:",
  "submit.qual.registeredLabel": "Registered on-chain.",
  "submit.qual.registeredBody": "Your address is a registered FTSO entity in Flare's reward data (required to list at all on Flare/Songbird).",
  "submit.qual.submittingLabel": "Submitting prices.",
  "submit.qual.submittingBody": "You are actively submitting in the latest reward epoch.",
  "submit.qual.votePowerLabel": "Sufficient vote power.",
  "submit.qual.votePowerBody": "Your vote power gives you a non-zero signing weight, so your submissions actually count toward consensus. Flare normalises vote power into a signing weight (your share of the total); a provider with too little vote power rounds to zero weight and does not count.",
  "submit.qual.uptimeLabel": "≥95% uptime over 30 days.",
  "submit.qual.uptimeBody": "Present in at least 95% of the last ~9 reward epochs (~30 days).",
  "submit.qual.addressLabel": "Address on your website.",
  "submit.qual.addressBody": "Your on-chain address is referenced on your site. Required for new providers; waived automatically once you have on-chain tenure (~30 days).",
  "submit.qual.oneLabel": "One provider per network.",
  "submit.qual.oneBody": "A single registered entity per network.",
  "submit.qual.keepTitle": "Keeping (and losing) Qualified status",
  "submit.qual.keepBody": "Qualified is {sticky}. Once you earn it, it stays, even if your vote power, uptime, or fee changes. There is exactly one way to lose it:",
  "submit.qual.sticky": "sticky",
  "submit.qual.loseLead": "Not submitting prices for 60 days (about 17 reward epochs).",
  "submit.qual.loseBody": "If you go that long without submitting, your Qualified status is revoked and you must re-qualify from scratch. Nothing else (a dip in any single metric) takes it away. The feed shows exactly how many epochs you have left before revocation, so it is never a surprise.",
  "submit.qual.selfDeclaredNote": "Items that cannot be verified on-chain (one entity per network, private node, in-house or open-source algorithm) are shown as self-declared. Learn {link}.",
  "submit.qual.selfDeclaredLink": "more about Flare Registry",
  "submit.warn.title": "Never share your private key or seed phrase.",
  "submit.warn.body": "Flare Registry will never ask for your private key, seed phrase, or recovery words, and you should never enter or send them anywhere. You only ever sign a message in your wallet to prove control of an address; signing reveals nothing secret.",
  "submit.which.title": "Which address should I use?",
  "submit.which.body": "An FTSO entity registers several addresses (identity, submit, submit-signatures, signing-policy and delegation). {identity} is recognised, so connect whichever wallet is most convenient and that you are comfortable signing with. Signing only proves control of the address; it never moves funds or reveals anything secret.",
  "submit.which.identity": "Any of your five registered addresses",
  "submit.contracts.summary": "Interacting on-chain? Flare contract addresses",
  "submit.contracts.intro": "If you prefer to register and manage your FTSO entity by calling the contracts directly, these are Flare's on-chain protocol contracts for each network, resolved live from the Flare Contract Registry.",
  "submit.contracts.disclaimer": "These are Flare protocol contracts, not flareregistry contracts. flareregistry is a directory: your listing here is always claimed and managed by signing, and we never broker on-chain actions.",
